WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:10.460
In 1977, a survey found only 33 pairs of bald eagles nesting in Virginia.

2
00:00:11.340 --> 00:00:16.500
In 2016, a larger search counted 1,070 pairs.

3
00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:19.800
A pair is two adults who use a nest.

4
00:00:20.660 --> 00:00:24.160
The larger search means the two counts are not a perfect match.

5
00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:27.880
Can people help a damaged ecosystem come back?

6
00:00:28.733 --> 00:00:33.473
A pesticide is a chemical used to kill pests, such as insects.

7
00:00:34.713 --> 00:00:37.913
DDT was a common pesticide in the United States.

8
00:00:39.013 --> 00:00:43.153
DDT breaks down into a related chemical called DDE.

9
00:00:44.313 --> 00:00:47.093
DDE can make bird eggshells thin.

10
00:00:48.273 --> 00:00:52.233
Very thin eagle eggshells often broke while the parents sat on them.

11
00:00:52.873 --> 00:00:54.293
Other eggs failed to hatch.

12
00:00:54.933 --> 00:00:57.093
So few young eagles were raised.

13
00:00:57.967 --> 00:01:00.927
DDT was not the only problem.

14
00:01:01.707 --> 00:01:05.887
People also destroyed eagle habitat, the place where eagles live.

15
00:01:06.867 --> 00:01:08.167
Then people acted.

16
00:01:09.047 --> 00:01:14.047
In 1972, the United States banned most uses of DDT.

17
00:01:15.027 --> 00:01:17.087
Laws protected eagles and their nests.

18
00:01:17.987 --> 00:01:20.107
People protected the places where eagles nest.

19
00:01:21.247 --> 00:01:25.867
Protecting living things and their habitats so they last is called conservation.

20
00:01:26.900 --> 00:01:29.100
Recovery took decades.

21
00:01:29.960 --> 00:01:33.480
Young eagles take several years to grow old enough to breed.

22
00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:38.220
New pairs raise young, and those young become pairs too.

23
00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:42.400
But eagles also die and face new dangers.

24
00:01:43.250 --> 00:01:47.090
Restoration is helping a damaged ecosystem recover.

25
00:01:48.210 --> 00:01:54.270
By 1933, a disease and a hurricane had wiped out eelgrass in Virginia's coastal

26
00:01:54.270 --> 00:01:58.470
bays. Scientists spread eelgrass seeds by hand.

27
00:01:59.310 --> 00:02:02.810
The new plants made seeds that spread past the planted areas.

28
00:02:03.830 --> 00:02:09.090
A 2020 study reported 3,612 hectares of eelgrass.

29
00:02:09.983 --> 00:02:11.803
Recovery has limits.

30
00:02:12.583 --> 00:02:17.403
A review of 400 studies found that damaged places often improve.

31
00:02:18.303 --> 00:02:21.423
Full recovery was less common while scientists watched.

32
00:02:22.143 --> 00:02:25.383
A recovered place can also look different from before.

33
00:02:26.183 --> 00:02:29.223
So can people help a damaged ecosystem come back?

34
00:02:29.843 --> 00:02:33.823
Yes. They can remove the cause, protect, and restore.

35
00:02:34.663 --> 00:02:38.383
But recovery is often slow, partial and different.
